          "text-align": "justify"
        },
        "table": null,
        "text": "Understanding Alphabet’s Financial Results",
        "text_hash": "a2d230ed93ed9b1c0a8886f4081b511e7ec480abfc459c2785fcba002c3b9cd9",
        "type": "heading_candidate"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000398-132d42ca",
        "dom_path": "/html/body/div[420]",
        "image_asset_id": null,
        "layout_role": null,
        "ordinal": 398,
        "reported_page": 28,
        "source_anchor": "i6be430fe3ebf411481dcec8b0abe9149_76",
        "style_signature": {
          "font-family": "'arial',sans-serif",
          "font-size": "10pt",
          "font-weight": "400",
          "line-height": "115%",
          "margin-top": "6pt",
          "text-align": "justify",
          "text-indent": "22.5pt"
        },
        "table": null,
        "text": "Alphabet is a collection of businesses — the largest of which is Google. We report Google in two segments, Google Services and Google Cloud, and all non-Google businesses collectively as Other Bets. Supporting these businesses, we have centralized certain AI-related research and development focused on advanced research in AI and developing the frontier models that serve our businesses, which is reported in Alphabet-level activities. For further details on our segments, see Part I, Item 1 Business and Note 15 of the Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements included in Item 8 of this Annual Report on Form 10-K.",
        "text_hash": "132d42cab8848e047d780963ba92b2c7ba3a6d864592965c24dc7bdbba63b893",
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
